{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted","id":584623,"title":"Touchstone-based Clan Banes? Feedback wanted.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T06:36:01-07:00","id":584623,"title":"Touchstone-based Clan Banes? Feedback wanted.","content":"I've been mulling over the Clan Banes for some time, now. Reading through several threads that touch that topic got me thinking about what I want from a Clan Bane and what a cool common underlying theme or mood might be.<br /> <br /> I came to the following conclusion:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A Clan Bane should symbolize a certain difficulty that members of the Clan share (no surprise here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</li> <li>It should leave a character with two options: give into it and cope with the consequences or struggle against it</li> <li>The latter option (and possibly the first one, too) should result in role playing opportunities: the character changes his/her behaviour to struggle against/cope with it.</li> <li>The underlying theme should correspond to what my players and I want it to be in our game. For us, this should be the struggle to uphold Humanity.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <b><u>Touchstones</u></b><br /> <br /> Ironically, the Ventrue Bane, while being widely regarded as a failure, fits<br /> this (almost) perfectly. With a few tweaks to the touchstone rules, it was fine.<br /> Then I tried to draft touchstone-based clan banes for the other clans, as well.<br /> <br /> First, the tweaked touchstone rules:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Slots for touchstones go from Humanity 6 to 1 and are filled from the top.</li> <li>Touchstones have two properties that can be true or false: &quot;Active&quot; and &quot;Attached&quot;.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>To be <b>active</b> means the touchstone currently fills a slot. To be active, the touchstone must be available (e.g. not dead as part of a story) and maintained by the character. Maintaining a touchstone requires regular meaningful interaction with it. What &quot;regular&quot; means in this context is up to the storyteller. Once per fortnight might be a good guideline.</li> <li>To be <b>attached</b>, the character needs to have a dot of Humanity at the slot of an active touchstone.</li> </ol></li> <li>The free touchstone every character begins with is protected by the &quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot;, too.</li> <li>Unattached touchstones need to be maintained, too, if a character wants to benefit from other touchstones.</li> <li>If a touchstone becomes inactive, other touchstones residing in lower slots move up to fill the gap.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> John Doe has two touchstones (in slots 6 and 5). As long as he stays at Humanity 6 or above, and maintains them, both are attached and active, so he benefits from the +3 bonus to detachment rolls. Eventually, his Humanity drops to 5. Now, both of his touchstones are still active, but only one is attached. He now only benefits from the +2 bonus. To keep that bonus, he still has to maintain regular contact with [em]both[/em] touchstones. Should he neglect his touchstone at 6, it becomes inactive and vacates the slot at Humanity 6. John's touchstone at 5 moves up to fill that slot. Now one of his touchstones is inactive (currently not filling a slot), and the other one is active, but not attached. So he loses his bonus. Should John make up with his inactive touchstone or establish a new one, this newly activated touchstone fills up the highest free slot (5). Now, John has an attached touchstone again and benefits from the +2 bonus. If he manages to raise his humanity to 6 again, he benefits from the +3 bonus.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ventrue Clan Bane</u></b><br /> <br /> With the rules above, the Ventrue Bane can remain as written in the book. The Beast of a Ventrue is an alpha. It is arrogant and feels superior, especially towards humans.<br /> <br /> This essentially means that the slots for touchstones don't go from Humanity 6 to 1, but from 7 to 2. That means, to gain the same bonuses to detachment rolls, a Ventrue must maintain one more touchstone than other clans.<br /> <br /> The effect of this is that due to their superiority complex, Ventrue must invest more experience and time into upholding their Humanity. Because they tend to view humans as beneath them, they have to struggle not to lose their contact to humanity.<br /> <br /> Ventrue either work at staying in contact to Humanity or they will detach more quickly than other clans.<br /> <br /> <b>So, to align the other Clan Banes, I'm looking for Humanity-related effects that cause trouble but can be &quot;contained&quot; by buying one additional touchstone and maintaining it.</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Gangrel Clan Bane</u></b><br /> <br /> The beat of a Gangrel is a particularly feral one. Once Gangrel hit Humanity 6, their dice pool to [em]resist[/em] frenzy (not the dice pool to ride the wave) is penalized by -2. For every attached touchstone, this penalty is reduced by one (but it doesn't turn into a bonus...).<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> Jane Gangrel has Humanity 6 and two active (and thus, attached) touchstones. She is not suffering any penalty on rolls to prevent frenzy. If her Humanity drops to 5, she either suffers a -1 penalty or she can try to build a stronger connection to her Humanity by establishing a third touchstone.<br /> <br /> Gangrel either work at staying in contact to Humanity or they will frenzy more often than other clans.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nosferatu Clan Bane</u></b><br /> <br /> The Beast of the Nosferatu is a terrifying thing. Once a Nosferatu hits Humanity 6, their effective Humanity for rolls to relate to humans is considered to be two steps lower. For every attached touchstone, this penalty is reduced by one (but it doesn't turn into a bonus...).<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> John Nosferatu has Humanity 6 and two active (and thus, attached) touchstones. For rolls to relate to humans, his Humanity is considered to be 6. No penalty. One of his touchstones becomes inactive (maybe he or she dies). Now John's Humanity is considered to be 5 until he can reconnect to humankind by activating his second touchstone.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu either work at staying in contact to Humanity or they will become unsettling towards humans more quickly than other clans.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mekhet Clan Bane</u></b><br /> <br /> The Mekhet Beast is a thing of the shadows. Once a Mekhet hits Humanity 6, his Humanity is considered to be one step lower in regard to Humanity-based banes (including sunlight and torpor). As long as the Mekhet has more than one attached touchstone, this penalty is neutralized.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> Jane Mekhet has Humanity 6 and two active (and thus, attached) touchstones. She is exposed to the sun. When determining the damage, her Humanity is considered to be 6. No penalty. Had one of her touchstones been inactive, her Humanity would have been considered 5.<br /> <br /> Mekhet either work at staying in contact to Humanity or they will become more vulnerable to sunlight and other Humanity-base banes more quickly than other clans.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Daeva Clan Bane</u></b><br /> <br /> The Daeva Beast is a thing of compulsion. Once Daeva hits Humanity 6, they tend to become obsessively attached to his or her touchstone and acquires the Persistent Dependent Condition toward the touchstone. Should the touchstone die while the Daeva is under that condition towards it, the Daeva immediately gains the Languid Condition.<br /> <br /> If a Daeva has more than one touchstone, the obsession is weakened enough to lose (not resolve) the Persistent Dependent Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> John Daeva has Humanity 6 and two active (and thus, attached) touchstones. He might be a little obsessed with his touchstones, but it doesn't have any effect in terms of game mechanics. If on of his touchstones becomes inactive, his obsession towards the remaining attached touchstone intensifies. He gains the Persistent Dependent Condition toward the touchstone.<br /> <br /> Once he reactivates his second touchstone, he loses the Persistent Dependent Condition. However, it is not &quot;resolved&quot;, it might come back, anytime. So he doesn't take a beat.<br /> <br /> Daeva either work at maintaining a broad contact to Humanity or they will become obsessed with their touchstones.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> What do you think? I'd be grateful for feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:15:26-07:00","id":584703,"title":"","content":"I like the thought process going on here, but I'll admit I sort of dislike the idea of having Touchstones mitigate Clan Banes. For one, I think that giving that in addition to the dice pool bonus they give to Humanity checks makes them almost <i>too </i>valuable for players, and makes it less likely that those banes come into play. Like the Nosferatu Clan Bane for instance is basically a non-issue with 1 Touchstone for 7-5, combined with the dice bonus it offers which will bulwark a lot of characters against degenerating unless you introduce additional kinds of modifiers (not a bad idea IMO)<br /> <br /> I think the philosophy of having touchstones interact with Clan Banes is a valuable one, but IMO the best way to get Clan Banes that aren't ignored constantly by those with Touchstones that beat Humanity rolls and is to find something that is either a common component of the vampiric condition (ex. the Mekhet Bane or the Gangrel Bane) or one that interacts with the character of the Clan (Nos are penalized when interacting with humans in most constructive ways BESIDES using fear and revulsion, like through Nightmare).<br /> <br /> I think the one issue with the Ventrue Clan Bane or the Daeva one is that they can feel a bit more passive than the others, even if the idea or the theme of it is compelling for the Clan.<br /> <br /> I think the Daeva Clan Bane is interesting and a creative way to re-do their dependency, while the Mekhet one loses out on the coolness of each Mekhet having their own weird little Bane. Ventrue makes sense within your framework, but I still wish there was some more substance there. I like the Gangrel one, sorta. Particularly the notion that their bane doesn't affect Riding the Wave. If anything, it feels like the Gangrel intimacy with the Beast should somehow make it easier, but the Bane isn't the place to discuss that.<br /> <br /> I think the Nosferatu one is the only one I really dislike, on account of it mitigating the penalties they suffer to social stuff (it makes no mention of the dramatic failures issue, which is another part of the bane)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:12:01-07:00","id":584820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584703#post584703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Mekhet one loses out on the coolness of each Mekhet having their own weird little Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the things I like about Quinn's system. It's always kind of irked me that the Mekhet got, in effect, three clan banes: extra damage from fire &amp; sunlight (and other banes where applicable), plus an extra bane, plus faster degeneration due the inability to take one of the three banes other clans are allowed. I typically tweak the Mekhet to only take the extra damage. <br /> <br /> You can still get the weirdness/coolness factor with <b>any</b> clan, just by taking interesting banes for a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:43:46-07:00","id":584872,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the idea that each Mekhet has a hidden weakness that hurts them worse than it could hurt the other Clans is a boon to the whole keeper and stealer of secrets thing they've got going on. Like yeah, your Daeva might be afraid of Church Bells, but it doesn't have quite the same <i>je ne sais quoi </i>as the clan that deals in secrets always having a secret of their own.<br /> <br /> Besides, you might not <i>know </i>the Daeva has a peculiar bane, but you <i>do </i>know theoretically that the Mekhet does, so it comes down to a matter of what, which can be a cool queue for players to work off of, and for the Mekhet player to develop for their Bane.<br /> <br /> That it means you can't take an additional Bane feels like another bite of the Bane that interacts with the Kindred Condition. I think that's kinda cool, but YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:01:02-07:00","id":584882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584872#post584872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea that each Mekhet has a hidden weakness that hurts them worse than it could hurt the other Clans is a boon to the whole keeper and stealer of secrets thing</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, but that's still stacking extra banes on one particular Clan. I'd rather the &quot;secret bane&quot; be the only clan bane they have instead of the extra damage from banes, or at least not make the extra bane count against the three they can take to mitigate degeneration. I guess I'd like to see a clear choice between the literal &quot;Shadow&quot; aspect of the clan (banished by light) and the metaphorical &quot;Shadow&quot; aspect of the clan (hidden and secret), instead of making both a source of weakness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:11:13-07:00","id":584909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584882#post584882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point, but that's still stacking extra banes on one particular Clan. I'd rather the &quot;secret bane&quot; be the only clan bane they have instead of the extra damage from banes, or at least not make the extra bane count against the three they can take to mitigate degeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's what makes it the Mekhet weakness as opposed to being just any old Bane. Whatever their secret bane is, it hurts them worse than other vampires. If you <i>had </i>to, I guess you could just make it so their Humanity only counts as lower for the Bane they take, but IMO that's less fun and... present than Mekhet being affected by the concept of banes more severely. <br /> <br /> Like, out of all the weaknesses, ones like the Mekhet one or the Nosferatu one or the Gangrel one feel the most &quot;present&quot; in a game, which is really neat. I like the idea of the Daeva one, but wish there was a better way to implement it. I think this way captures one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584882#post584882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'd like to see a clear choice between the literal &quot;Shadow&quot; aspect of the clan (banished by light) and the metaphorical &quot;Shadow&quot; aspect of the clan (hidden and secret), instead of making both a source of weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That those two things go together makes a lot of sense to me, but that's WoD metaphysics for you, they almost always seem to be operating on ideas of conceptual sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:03:04-07:00","id":584981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584909#post584909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That those two things go together makes a lot of sense to me, but that's WoD metaphysics for you, they almost always seem to be operating on ideas of conceptual sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol, very true. I'm just being pissy about it because Mekhet are my favorite clan and I always thought B&amp;S kind of screwed them on the banes. Now, to circle this very derailed thread back...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think? I'd be grateful for feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like what you did with the Daeva, since it seems to imply that as they lose humanity it's their touchstones who can still make them <b>feel </b>human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:51:08-07:00","id":585133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584703#post584703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, I think that giving that in addition to the dice pool bonus they give to Humanity checks makes them almost <i>too </i>valuable for players, and makes it less likely that those banes come into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think so? As soon as Humanity starts to drop, stuff get's really complicated. Let's say you drop to 4. In order to avoid your clan bane,<br /> you have to maintain 4 touchstones. That's a lot of work, and a lot of commitment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584703#post584703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the Nosferatu Clan Bane for instance is basically a non-issue with 1 Touchstone for 7-5, combined with the dice bonus it offers which will bulwark a lot of characters against degenerating unless you introduce additional kinds of modifiers (not a bad idea IMO)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite get it. What do you mean by &quot;1 Touchstone for 7-5&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584703#post584703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while the Mekhet one loses out on the coolness of each Mekhet having their own weird little Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I never liked that very much. I never even considered using that part of their Clan Bane.<br /> <br /> But I'm not quite happy with the whole system of taking Banes in exchange for immunity to breaking points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584703#post584703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Nosferatu one is the only one I really dislike, on account of it mitigating the penalties they suffer to social stuff (it makes no mention of the dramatic failures issue, which is another part of the bane)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I completely forgot the dramatic failures when drafting this. I think I would still leave it out, but it wouldn't break anything to put it back in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584872#post584872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but the idea that each Mekhet has a hidden weakness that hurts them worse than it could hurt the other Clans is a boon to the whole keeper and stealer of secrets thing they've got going on. Like yeah, your Daeva might be afraid of Church Bells, but it doesn't have quite the same <i>je ne sais quoi </i>as the clan that deals in secrets always having a secret of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never thought of it that way, cool thought. However, you don't need a Bane for that. Knowing secrets is a secret of it own. Imagine you know this crime lord is cheating on his wife, which he really doesn't want to come out. Your first priority is that he doesn't know that you know, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=584981#post584981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like what you did with the Daeva, since it seems to imply that as they lose humanity it's their touchstones who can still make them <b>feel </b>human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It was just a side effect of modeling something that would be remedied by a secound touchstone. But I like it, too, especially that their obsession and dependency is now towards their touchstones and not to just everyone they feed more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:36:14-07:00","id":585208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think so? As soon as Humanity starts to drop, stuff get's really complicated. Let's say you drop to 4. In order to avoid your clan bane,<br /> you have to maintain 4 touchstones. That's a lot of work, and a lot of commitment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my practical experience with the game has shown me that a player character getting to Humanity 4 either requires neglecting your touchstones or detachment rolls out the ass. My players role frequently, and I've run a couple of games now since Blood &amp; Smoke came out, and one pretty consistent thing is that, thanks to Touchstones it's actually pretty hard to lose Humanity, even if you're rolling against Humanity 2 almost every time.<br /> <br /> So it's not that I disagree, so much as I think players won't let their Humanity drop like that, especially players that want that mechanical incentive for multiple touchstones and want to avoid a merit tax. I'm not really taking an adversarial approach to GMing here, although that last sentence might sound it, but it can be an issue.<br /> <br /> It's also worth mentioning that, practically speaking, it's hard enough to do a game with a single touchstone for every player, if you're trying to give each of them their due. I imagine it'll be very logistically difficult as a GM to manage 4 touchstones for the player to interact with, nevermind the fact that you might wind up doing that for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite get it. What do you mean by &quot;1 Touchstone for 7-5&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to having 1 Touchstone at Humanity 7 through 5 completely negating their curse, which sort of predicates on my first point, that a lot of player characters will wind up in that range, meaning their Clan Curse actually won't come up unless &quot;disaster strikes&quot; (story happens) and they go lower or lose their touchstone. If the Clan Banes weren't supposed to be a part of the psychology of the characters then that wouldn't really matter, but if we're at the point where it isn't affecting their Requiem, it sort of hurts the character of the Clan, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I never liked that very much. I never even considered using that part of their Clan Bane.<br /> <br /> But I'm not quite happy with the whole system of taking Banes in exchange for immunity to breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well. If you don't like it for your game, I can hardly knock you for removing it. I just think it's a shame, since it adds just a little bit more weirdness to the Clan that can be a little fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I completely forgot the dramatic failures when drafting this. I think I would still leave it out, but it wouldn't break anything to put it back in.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my previous stuff about the Nosferatu. The Lonely Curse kind of stops being very Lonely if it doesn't affect them at all. If the Clan Banes contribute to the identity of the Kindred of the clan, neutralizing most of the drawbacks feels like a loss of story opportunities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought of it that way, cool thought. However, you don't need a Bane for that. Knowing secrets is a secret of it own. Imagine you know this crime lord is cheating on his wife, which he really doesn't want to come out. Your first priority is that he doesn't know that you know, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite the same thing, and isn't personal to the character the way a personal weakness can be. You also get that by way of Auspex, and isn't really an incentive to keep a secret. Like, him not knowing you know anything is part and parcel to the general experience of being Mekhet, but it's not a vulnerability to hide, and the situation is further complicated in Kindred scenarios, where people <i>know </i>the Mekhet <i>know </i>things, and they're already suspicious of you anyway. That the Mekhet will almost always have some kind of vicious weakness that can be exploited is a secret they have to keep, and a secret for others to go after.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't really work for you, that's too bad. I think the Bane you've got for them currently is perfectly adequate and serviceable within your system, if a bit unexciting, like the Mekhet Bane in 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585133#post585133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. It was just a side effect of modeling something that would be remedied by a secound touchstone. But I like it, too, especially that their obsession and dependency is now towards their touchstones and not to just everyone they feed more than once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Daeva clan bane is the one that sees the most success in this system, and the bit about the obsession being diffused among multiple Touchstones is pretty neat.<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, I think these are a decent hack for a Touchstone-centric chronicle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:23:11-07:00","id":585283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585208#post585208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my practical experience with the game has shown me that a player character getting to Humanity 4 either requires neglecting your touchstones or detachment rolls out the ass. My players role frequently, and I've run a couple of games now since Blood &amp; Smoke came out, and one pretty consistent thing is that, thanks to Touchstones it's actually pretty hard to lose Humanity, even if you're rolling against Humanity 2 almost every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't use a lot of situational modifiers for attachment rolls, right? I usually withhold detachment rolls until the end of the chapter and have the players roleplay a sort of debriefing with a touchstone. If they really get into the emotion of &quot;Oh my goodness, what has become of me?&quot;, they'll just roll unmodified or even get a small bonus. Else, they're really going to need that touchstone bonuses :-)<br /> <br /> But still, you got a point there. If they manage to keep up their they pretty much get off the Clan Bane hook. But that's fine with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585208#post585208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth mentioning that, practically speaking, it's hard enough to do a game with a single touchstone for every player, if you're trying to give each of them their due. I imagine it'll be very logistically difficult as a GM to manage 4 touchstones for the player to interact with, nevermind the fact that you might wind up doing that for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. It takes up a lot of time and probably only good for groups who like that. But it can be a lot of fun, especially when the players play other players' touchstones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585208#post585208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to having 1 Touchstone at Humanity 7 through 5 completely negating their curse, which sort of predicates on my first point, that a lot of player characters will wind up in that range, meaning their Clan Curse actually won't come up unless &quot;disaster strikes&quot; (story happens) and they go lower or lose their touchstone. If the Clan Banes weren't supposed to be a part of the psychology of the characters then that wouldn't really matter, but if we're at the point where it isn't affecting their Requiem, it sort of hurts the character of the Clan, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks for clearing that up. I agree, but I still think the Clan characteristics will come out in the *way* they struggle to contain the effects of their Banes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585208#post585208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not quite the same thing, and isn't personal to the character the way a personal weakness can be. You also get that by way of Auspex, and isn't really an incentive to keep a secret. Like, him not knowing you know anything is part and parcel to the general experience of being Mekhet, but it's not a vulnerability to hide, and the situation is further complicated in Kindred scenarios, where people <i>know </i>the Mekhet <i>know </i>things, and they're already suspicious of you anyway. That the Mekhet will almost always have some kind of vicious weakness that can be exploited is a secret they have to keep, and a secret for others to go after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:31:22-07:00","id":585287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585283#post585283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't use a lot of situational modifiers for attachment rolls, right? I usually withhold detachment rolls until the end of the chapter and have the players roleplay a sort of debriefing with a touchstone. If they really get into the emotion of &quot;Oh my goodness, what has become of me?&quot;, they'll just roll unmodified or even get a small bonus. Else, they're really going to need that touchstone bonuses :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wanting to use more situational modifiers as time goes on, it's just something I haven't figured out. Like, what would make compelling additional modifiers on top of the base ones (I dig the way Dirge/Mask can affect it, for instance!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585283#post585283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thanks for clearing that up. I agree, but I still think the Clan characteristics will come out in the *way* they struggle to contain the effects of their Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I think that's part of my struggle here. The Daeva one, you can clearly tell sort of how the Touchstone does affect the Clan Bane, the others are less clear, narrative-wise. Like I can clearly see the mechanical benefits that incentivize the keeping of Touchstones, but barring the Daeva one, I don't see how it differs from Clan to Clan.<br /> <br /> Like, Ventrue, Mekhet, Gangrel, Nosferatu, all they have to do is keep their Touchstones and they won't have to deal with their Clan Banes. The Daeva, you're giving in your description a sense of how the Touchstones mitigate the curse, and how the relationship with their Touchstone plays out the Daeva passion. I think that's why I favor that one the most of the bunch, because I'm not seeing the mechanic/narrative of how the other Clans struggle with their Clan Banes or how their Touchstones hook into them. I hope that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I think that kind of connecting how the Touchstones help mitigate the Curse in their descriptions would give them a stronger relationship. Think the Gangrel keeping his touchstones in his head as a sort of rock against getting swept away by the Red, or a Mekhet whose Touchstones help keep him real, preventing him from becoming an anonymous, Bane'd (???) creature sort of like Doe from the Clanbook, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> That'd help with the flavor of it, though it doesn't completely alleviate the issue of how one's Clan might be evoked through their touchstone relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-09-2015, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:54:14-07:00","id":585380,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I think the problem is twofold.<br /> <br /> First, you could rethink the system with another approach. Instead of thinking how they are affected by Banes when they are low on Touchstones, think about how the touchstones relate to them. The prob is, all clans become &quot;keep two active Touchstones, or else&quot;. As long as the player manages to keep high Humanity OR high number of Touchstones, he doesn't have any clan weakness.<br /> <br /> Second, the whole issue is that you have your own view about the game.<br /> <br /> Masquerade was a LOT about Humanity. Requiem isn't, not on the same touch, at least. In Requiem, it is about BLENDING. Just so you can have monstrous characters without problem. And so the game don't limit possible approachs on the characters.<br /> <br /> If you like the Masquerade approach, I think your Banes are good enough for you. You WANT to have a HUGE focus on keeping Humanity. No prob, but hardly good for most people.<br /> <br /> Be cautious only with the Banes-for-Sins thing. They're there for the same reason Masquerade had Paths. If you take that, you will have limits about the kinds of characters you can have. No inhuman villains or strange ways to see things, because on the botton of the well lies the Draugr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:39:33-07:00","id":585731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585287#post585287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva one, you can clearly tell sort of how the Touchstone does affect the Clan Bane, the others are less clear, narrative-wise. Like I can clearly see the mechanical benefits that incentivize the keeping of Touchstones, but barring the Daeva one, I don't see how it differs from Clan to Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see that. If I understand you right, the Daeva part of my draft has something outside the game mechanics that will give Daeva players an idea of how the struggle feels, right? An angle to go for in roleplaying the struggle?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'd like that for the others, too. That's something to think about. I'd be glad for suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585287#post585287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that kind of connecting how the Touchstones help mitigate the Curse in their descriptions would give them a stronger relationship. Think the Gangrel keeping his touchstones in his head as a sort of rock against getting swept away by the Red, or a Mekhet whose Touchstones help keep him real, preventing him from becoming an anonymous, Bane'd (???) creature sort of like Doe from the Clanbook, etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I especially like the Mekhet idea, that they need their touchstones to assure them they're even real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585380#post585380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you could rethink the system with another approach. Instead of thinking how they are affected by Banes when they are low on Touchstones, think about how the touchstones relate to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, sounds good, but I can't quite think of anything. Do you have an example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585380#post585380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the whole issue is that you have your own view about the game.<br /> <br /> Masquerade was a LOT about Humanity. Requiem isn't, not on the same touch, at least.<br /> *snip*<br /> If you like the Masquerade approach, I think your Banes are good enough for you. You WANT to have a HUGE focus on keeping Humanity. No prob, but hardly good for most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like the game to be about Humanity. The V:TM was talking a lot about it, but the game was actually pretty bad at letting you experience this theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=585380#post585380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be cautious only with the Banes-for-Sins thing. They're there for the same reason Masquerade had Paths. If you take that, you will have limits about the kinds of characters you can have. No inhuman villains or strange ways to see things, because on the botton of the well lies the Draugr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I see the necessity of it, too. I'm just not happy with it. From reading the first Anne Rice books, I loved that in this &quot;modern&quot; Vampire concept, all those stupid little banes like not being able to cross running water were gone. I'm not happy that they're coming back through the backdoor. But that can be remedied by working with the players to work out some banes that really fit the character without getting into too much clich\u00e9.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the feedback, so far, guys. Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","user":"Quinn","date":". 07-10-2015, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:25:20-07:00","id":585984,"title":"","content":"What if, rather than letting your Touchstones mitigate your Bane numerically, each Clan just treated Touchstones differently?<br /> <br /> For example, the Mekhet all receive a &quot;free&quot; Bane. They also gain the unique choice of making that Bane a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:21:43-07:00","id":586320,"title":"","content":"The Touchstone is a mark of your previous life. It SHOULD be detached of your clan, because it is about the Human, not the Beast. I think the Beast could TAINT the relation, instead of defining it.<br /> <br /> Maybe each &quot;Bane&quot; gives a willpower point for relating with the Touchstone in a way, but doing so reduces the bonus they give, or even eliminates them as Touchstones.<br /> <br /> Ventrue wants to relate in a domineering way, getting power OVER the Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Mekhet wants to be a ghost, knowing without being known.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu wants to be feared or cause disgust, for his Touchstone to know he's a nightmare.<br /> <br /> Gangrel wants to relate in survival terms, his Touchstone is Pack or Territory and must be defended and marked as such.<br /> <br /> Daeva wants to sense, to get the most pleasure from the relation, a passion that can overlook necessities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T04:41:39-07:00","id":591128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/584623-touchstone-based-clan-banes-feedback-wanted?p=586320#post586320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Touchstone is a mark of your previous life. It SHOULD be detached of your clan, because it is about the Human, not the Beast. I think the Beast could TAINT the relation, instead of defining it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that the Beast is trying to taint the relationship with Touchstones. In the past few days I've been thinking about a way to implement this into game mechanics. I came up with a few ideas, too. However, that could best be used as additional banes (e.g. in exchange for immunity towards a breaking point). If I'd replace the Clan Banes with that, they'd only apply to touchstones.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm more in favour of taking that idea and use it as &quot;soft&quot; roleplaying cues for interactions with their touchstones, e.g. to encourage Gangrel players to play up the conflict between the Man, who wants to connect to the Touchstone emotionally and the Beast, that wants to see the Touchstone as prey; to encourage Mekhet players to play up the interest of their Beast to lay open the secrets of their Touchstones instead of talking to them about their own morality issues etc.<br /> <br /> That might help to find a solution for the criticism that Leetsepeak has given. It might give the Clan Banes of Mekhet, Nosferatu and Gangrel, whose connection to Touchstones is not as visible as for Ventrue and Daeva a bit more flavour and substance.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}